  ('AUTO_TAGGING_SETTINGS', '{"reminders":{"enabled":false,"mode":"auto","tagIds":[]},"book_finished":{"enabled":false,"mode":"auto","tagIds":[]},"book_added":{"enabled":false,"mode":"suggest","tagIds":[]},"imdb_added":{"enabled":false,"mode":"suggest","tagIds":[]},"url_content":{"enabled":false,"mode":"suggest","tagIds":[]},"tag_search":{"enabled":false,"mode":"auto"},"ai_generated":{"enabled":false,"mode":"suggest"},"linked_note":{"enabled":false,"mode":"auto","tagIds":[]}}'),
  ('AI_MODEL_SUMMARIZE', 'gpt-4o-mini'),
  ('AI_MODEL_OCR', 'gpt-4o-mini'),
  ('AI_MODEL_REMINDER', 'o3-mini'),
  ('AI_MODEL_AUTO_TAG', 'gpt-4o'),
  ('AI_PROMPT_SUMMARIZE', 'Summarize the following text. The output is for my personal use as a high-density cognitive trigger, not for communication.\r\nRules:\r\nCondense to the absolute core. A few lines max.\r\nStrip out all communicative language, narrative, and transitional phrases (e.g., "this means," "in other words," "the author suggests").\r\nThe result should be raw data: the essential concepts, key phrases, and defining terms that will allow me to instantly recognize the text''s content. No wasted words.\r\nExample Transformation:\r\nInput-style thinking: "This led to the realization that the work of ''fixing'' is over."\r\nDesired Output: "Shift from fixing to living."\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT - don''t make it wordy.\r\ni want to be able to understand the structure of the note at a glance.'),
  ('AI_PROMPT_SUMMARIZE_CUSTOM', ''),
  ('AI_PROMPT_OCR', ''),
  ('AI_PROMPT_OCR_CUSTOM', ''),
  ('AI_PROMPT_REMINDER', 'Analyze the following text and identify the user''s reminder request.\r\n\r\nTask:\r\n1. Determine the target "wall clock" time in the user''s timezone.\r\n2. Identify the correct timezone offset for that date/location (e.g. +02:00 or +03:00).\r\n3. Return the "next_run_at" as an ISO 8601 string **including the numeric offset** (e.g. "2025-12-09T14:30:00+02:00").\r\n4. DO NOT return a ''Z'' (UTC) ending unless the offset is truly +00:00. Use the local time + offset format.\r\n5. CRITICAL - NEXT_RUN_AT DATE LOGIC (READ CAREFULLY):\r\n   The "next_run_at" must be the SOONEST FUTURE occurrence. Compare the requested date to the Current Time.\r\n   - If user says "Dec 16" and current date is Dec 15, 2025 → next_run_at = 2025-12-16 (THIS YEAR, tomorrow!)\r\n   - If user says "Dec 14" and current date is Dec 15, 2025 → next_run_at = 2026-12-14 (next year, since Dec 14 already passed)\r\n   - If user says "Jan 5" and current date is Dec 15, 2025 → next_run_at = 2026-01-05 (next year, since Jan 5 2025 already passed)\r\n   THIS APPLIES TO BOTH ONE-TIME AND RECURRING REMINDERS. For recurring, next_run_at is the FIRST occurrence.\r\n   DO NOT automatically add a year just because we''re in December. Check if the date has passed or not!\r\n\r\nReturn JSON:\r\n- "rrule": (string|null) RRULE string for recurring reminders. MUST be complete and specific:\r\n   * For yearly recurrence: MUST include BYMONTH and BYMONTHDAY. Example: "FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=12;BYMONTHDAY=20"\r\n   * For monthly recurrence: MUST include BYMONTHDAY. Example: "FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15"\r\n   * For weekly recurrence: MUST include BYDAY. Example: "FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,WE,FR"\r\n   * NEVER return just "FREQ=YEARLY" or "FREQ=MONTHLY" alone - always include the specific day/month components.\r\n- "next_run_at": (string) The target time ISO string WITH OFFSET.\r\n- "matched_text": (string) The EXACT substring from the input that encompasses the ENTIRE reminder request (both the scheduling command AND the content).\r\n- "reformatted_content": (string) The user''s core intent text, rephrased naturally without the scheduling part.\r\n- "schedule_summary": (string|null) For recurring reminders only, a short human-readable description of the schedule (e.g. "Every year on July 18"). Null for one-time reminders.\r\n- "type": (string) "recurring" or "one-time".\r\nIf no reminder is found, return { "error": "No reminder found" }.'),
  ('AI_PROMPT_REMINDER_CUSTOM', ''),
  ('AI_PROMPT_AUTO_TAG', 'You are a helpful assistant that categorizes notes.\r\n\r\nTask:\r\nSelect up to 3 of the most relevant tags from the available list for this note.\r\nIMPORTANT: Focus on EXPLICIT aspects mentioned in the note (specific topics, names, projects, etc.), NOT general themes.\r\nAvoid broad thematic tags that could apply to many notes - choose tags that create distinction and specificity.\r\nOnly select tags that are directly and explicitly referenced in the note content.\r\n\r\nOutput Format:\r\nReturn a JSON object with a single key "tags" containing an array of strings (the names of the selected tags).\r\nExample: { "tags": ["client-acme", "q4-2025"] }\r\nIf no tags are relevant, return { "tags": [] }.'),
  ('AI_PROMPT_AUTO_TAG_CUSTOM', '')
